from protesters to police officers  appeared to be shifting strategy today  as police worked to clear the remaining  protesters from the area the slow  methodical approach that we saw from  police yesterday seemed to be replaced  with a much tougher line today our auto  bureau chief mercedes stephenson has  been on the ground today so mercedes  what did you make of the police tactics  you saw today  jeff it felt very different from  yesterday where things started out very  slowly the officers who were on the  front line yesterday were just in their  regular uniforms they didn't have  additional body armor helmets on today  it was clear there was a different tone  being set the officers who came out  were wearing riot gear they were on the  front lines and they were carrying large  wooden batons with them which they were  using to strike people if they didn't  move back when the police line moved  forward they also had gas masks in some  cases and eventually the line that i got  pushed back by  on a side street here had full-blown gas  masks under riot helmets which led  people to believe they were going to be  gassed that never happened by the way  despite social media reports about it  there was a much faster pace that was  undertaken by the officers  it was more aggressive and there was a  harder element right behind them the  emergency response team who are tactical  officers with the rcmp very elite unit  were being used to clear out the tents  and also being used to clear out the  trucks and they had their weapons out  and drawn i did not see them pointing  them at anybody but it certainly was a  much more aggressive presence and it was  much more rapid they cleared all of  wellington street in the side streets in  a day in something that experts thought  might take as long as a week to do  yeah we heard the statement from the  police chief earlier citing concerns  about misinformation disinformation  circulating on social media how would  you describe you know what you're seeing  online versus the reality there on the  ground  yeah there were some people alleging  police brutality i didn't see that i did  see people absolutely getting hit by  batons and some rough arrests those were  people who did not move back as the  police line advanced sometimes they were  on their knees  begging with officers some veterans  saying please don't do this but if you  did not move when they told you to move  that was the fate that you suffered  there was no gas used nobody was shot  there was not mass arrests at gun points  despite what a new york times headline  appeared to report and most importantly  no one died because there was a false  report on american news that a woman was  trampled by a horse yesterday that did  not happen that was confirmed by both  police and ems but the police chief did  talk today about the problem they've had  with misinformation and disinformation  this is what he had to say one of the  tactics that the protesters and  demonstrators are using is  misinformation  information that is inaccurate  information that misleads the public  we're actively tweeting and providing  information out in through social media  and other media  mechanisms in order to be able to try  and get accurate factual information  around what is going on within the  protest  so jeff certainly a more aggressive  police presence and the possibility you  could get hurt if you did not move back  when the police instructed you to but  nothing like some of the other riot  police i've seen in action in the past  including at the g7 g20 which was much  more aggressive tactics  mercedes-stevenson in ottawa thanks  mercedes
 

